{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Third confirmed occurrence — and it settles the fix direction\n\nReproduced again, independently, closing `electronic-deducible-maggot`. Two edges to the same\ntarget, distinguishable by link id:\n\n- `8b828d0a` — written earlier by `rebar link <bug> <origin> caused_by`\n- `93b33884` — written by the close's `--caused-by`\n\n`rebar unlink <bug> <origin> caused_by` removed **precisely one**, leaving one. That is now 3/3\nreproductions and 3/3 successful repairs, so both the trigger and the remedy are reliable.\n\n## The important part: passing the flag is still CORRECT\n\nThe tempting reading of this bug is \"stop passing `--caused-by` when a link already exists.\" That\nwould be wrong, and this occurrence demonstrates why concretely.\n\nHad the close been made with an EMPTY `--caused-by`, blame auto-derivation would have run\nunconditionally and named a **June file-move carrier in `test_cli.py`** — a file whose lines\npredate the behaviour change entirely. The proven origin is `8d36-a15a-fcbd-4ebd`, reached through\nthe unmet-obligation path: a later change altered test-distribution assumptions without updating\nthe tests that relied on the marker. Blame cannot find that, by construction.\n\nSo the two failure modes are NOT symmetric:\n\n| | edge written | metric effect |\n|---|---|---|\n| pass the flag with an existing link | duplicate, **correct** target | one escape counted twice |\n| omit the flag | **wrong** target, silently | one escape charged to an innocent ticket |\n\nA duplicate correct edge is recoverable and visibly wrong. A single wrong edge is neither — it\nlooks exactly like a considered attribution. **The guidance to always pass the flag should stand;\nthe defect is that the write is not idempotent.**\n\nThat resolves the \"Direction\" section's open question in favour of making the `--caused-by` write\nidempotent for an identical `(relation, target)` pair, and against the alternative remedy of\namending the `/rebar-debug` guidance to stop prescribing the combination. Amending the guidance\nwould trade a clean invariant for a rule agents must remember, AND would reintroduce the\nstrictly worse wrong-edge failure mode.\n\n## Corroborating pattern\n\nThis is the fourth attribution today to resolve as an unmet obligation where naive blame would\nhave named the wrong ticket (the others: `fc20` for the disposition gate, `789c` for the dedup\nconsumer, `c1de` for the write-path drain gate). In every one, the fix site was not the cause site.\nThat is the exact case the escape metric most needs to get right, and the case where an empty\n`--caused-by` is most dangerous — which is why the duplicate is the cheaper of the two failures to\ntolerate while this is unfixed.\n\nEvidence supplied by the agent that closed `electronic-deducible-maggot`; it flagged rather than\nwrote, since another ticket's RCA is outside its pre-approved writebacks."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787266626099796001,"uuid":"3e4af083-4beb-4531-8f94-77aa0e402025"}